"La version la plus répandue évoque un vieux soldat, ancien sergent, qui vivait au bord du lac. Une autre hypothèse le rattache au mot serre-joint, un outil dont le lac aurait la forme.": "The most common version refers to an old soldier, a former sergeant, who lived on the lakeshore. Another theory links it to serre-joint, a clamp whose shape the lake is said to resemble.",
